<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  The add-on support is gated here rather than by MayRequire on every def, and rather than by
  PatchOperationFindMod, which the original mod used in three of its five patch files.
  PatchOperationFindMod compares a mod's *display name*, not its packageId, so it silently stops
  matching the day an author renames the workshop item - and the Sushi add-on is exactly the kind
  of mod that gets renamed. IfModActive compares packageIds, which do not change.

  It also settles the Sushi add-on's two 1.6 folders (1.6Odyssey and 1.6NotOdyssey) for free:
  patches run against the finished document, after Sushi's own loadFolders has picked one of
  them, so a single patch serves both cases and never has to know which one loaded.

  Kit's Brazilian Crops needs the Stews add-on as well as Brazilian Crops itself: the recipes it
  hangs off are gated on VCE_StewCooking, a research project that lives in Stews, and the uncooked
  stew textures live there too. The original mod guarded on Brazilian Crops alone, which left an
  unresolved research reference for anyone running Brazilian Crops without Stews.
-->
<loadFolders>
	<v1.6>
		<li>/</li>
		<li IfModActive="VanillaExpanded.VCookEStews">Mods/Stews</li>
		<li IfModActive="VanillaExpanded.VCookESushi">Mods/Sushi</li>
		<li IfModActiveAll="zal.braziliancrops,VanillaExpanded.VCookEStews">Mods/BrazilianCrops</li>
	</v1.6>
</loadFolders>
